            {
              "id": "F6",
              "kind": "suspected_slowdown",
              "family": "many_distinct_specifier_sets_few_specifiers_hashed_once",
              "why": "Even with only a few specifiers per set, the head version still pays the one‑time sort (k log k) on the first hash/equality, while the old frozenset hash is O(k). When a large number (n) of distinct sets are inserted into a set/dict, the extra log factor accumulates.",
              "size_meaning": "n = number of distinct SpecifierSet objects; each contains a fixed small number (e.g. 4) of specifiers. Total work grows ~ n·log k vs n·k.",
              "make_source": "def make(n):\n    \"\"\"Return n argument‑lists, each with a unique 4‑clause specifier string.\"\"\"\n    specs = []\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        parts = [f\">={i}.0\", f\"!={i+10}.0\", f\">={i+20}.0\", f\"!={i+30}.0\"]\n        specs.append([\",\".join(parts)])\n    return specs",
